# Mission Control — what must never enter git history.
#
# This file is a security control, not housekeeping. The repo has no remote today, but
# private-to-public is a decision someone can make later and history is not editable in
# practice: anything committed once is committed for good. So the rule is to exclude by
# CATEGORY (anything holding real money, health or credential data) rather than by
# filename, and to re-check when a new directory appears.

# --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The LAN access key. Minted on first boot; committing it would publish the gate.
data/gate-key.txt

# Google OAuth (#9). BY CATEGORY, and written BEFORE either file could exist — a
# credential that is committed once is committed for good, and the window in which the
# rule is missing is the window in which it gets committed.
#   data/google-client.json  the OAuth client you download from Google Cloud Console
#   data/google-token.json   the refresh token, written after you grant consent
# A refresh token is a long-lived key to a live mailbox. It is worth more than the LAN
# gate key above, because revoking it needs Google's console rather than deleting a file.
data/google-client.json
data/google-token.json
# Multi-account form, keyed by email. Added BEFORE the file could exist, 18 Aug — the
# window in which the rule is missing is the window in which it gets committed.
data/google-tokens.json
data/oauth-*.json

# --- real financial and personal data ----------------------------------------------
# dashboard.db holds ten account-years — 6,839 real bank transactions — plus health
# metrics and the wellbeing journal. The -wal and -shm files hold the same data mid-write.
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal

# Universal Credit statements, parsed from the PDFs on the owner's desktop. Each record
# carries the award breakdown, the deductions, the rent and service charges AND the home
# address off the statement head. This is not merely financial, it is benefit and health
# data — LCWRA is on every row — so it is excluded by name rather than left to a *.db rule
# that would never have matched a .jsonl.
data/uc-statements.jsonl

# 41 MB of VACUUM INTO copies of exactly the same thing.
/backups/

# Session telemetry for this workspace (backlog #6). Derived metrics about sessions that
# read the bank ledger; the owner chose gitignored over committed on 18 Aug.
data/telemetry/

# Runtime state, rewritten every 30s. Noise in a diff and useless in history.
data/heartbeat.json
data/watchdog-state.json

# Generated output that quotes the ledger: the daily briefing carries real spending
# figures and the tax reports carry five years of turnover. Both regenerate from the
# database on demand, so nothing is lost by keeping them out.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not style. A pattern without one matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so bare "reports/" was also excluding
# public/panels/reports/ -- the Reports PANEL, two files of source, silently never
# committed since git init. Found 18 Aug when git add refused the path. The same trap is
# waiting for logs/ and backups/, so those are anchored too.
/reports/

# --- logs --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Request and error logs can echo query strings and data values.
/logs/
*.log

# --- restorable ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# package-lock.json is committed; node_modules is not. One dependency, no native builds.
node_modules/

# --- os / editor ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   data/seed/     — the backlog seeder is code, and carries no transaction data
#   package-lock.json — pins the one dependency
#   CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md — the reasoning is the most valuable thing here

# Honeygain API bearer token. Ignored BEFORE the file exists, so it can never be
# accidentally committed in the window between creating it and remembering to ignore it.
data/honeygain-token.txt
data/*-token.txt

# The HOLLOWMAST dash proxy password. Ignored before the file exists.
data/dash-password.txt

# Credentials for the stats sources, ignored BEFORE they can exist. The order is the safety
# property: the dangerous window is the minute between creating a credential file and
# remembering to ignore it, and that window is how a key gets committed for good.
data/reports-admin-key.txt
data/ga-service-account.json

# The passphrase for the encrypted off-machine backup. Never committed.
data/backup-key.txt
